@@ -42,3 +42,8 @@ T0021 adds an explicit **`model_family: dense-ntp`** path to the existing experi
 The dense objective is final NTP only: `Objective.total = final_ntp`, with early/offset/balance zero and `offset2_count = 0`. Dense configs have no dormant MTP head. Configs `configs/experiments/dense-ntp-512x6-q8kv4-ffn2432.json` (35,527,168 parameters) and `dense-ntp-512x6-q8kv2-ffn2176.json` (32,381,440) are planning candidates from accepted T0019, not trained or optimized results. `splot-nano-v16384-a0.json` pins the V16384 SPLOT A0 R2 comparator (36,763,620 total including dormant MTP, 36,615,780 NTP base) with explicit `balance_weight=0.01`.
 
 `tools/accounting.py` adds `DenseShape`/`dense_account` for per-document causal contraction counts; these are analytical MACs, not training FLOPs. `tools/test_dense_harness.py` covers exact counts, semantic partition, dense objective equality, continuous 4 vs 2+2 resume, cross-family rejection, shared data ingestion and CPU BF16 capability when available. No full training, real data, test access, FP8 dense path or GPU/MPS qualification is claimed.
+
+## T0023 actual-vocabulary pilot and matched-run preflight (2026-11-28)
+`pilot_ingestion` now preserves the legacy model vocabulary 32768 and additionally accepts the exact validated manifest vocabulary in the bounded 264–16384 range. Arbitrary padded sizes, noninteger/bool values, values below the manifest vocabulary and values other than 32768 or exact equality fail closed. Equal vocabulary reports `unused_token_id_count=0` and empty ranges; legacy 32768 keeps the original unused range. Test is still integrity-validated only and never returned.
+
+The dense objective uses the shared `splot.dense.ntp_loss` for FP32/BF16. Explicit `model_family` configs additionally report physical and gradient-present parameter tensors/numel and separate MTP/dormant-MTP inventory; legacy absent-family SPLOT reports remain unchanged. The V16384 tiny pilot CLI test runs A0 dense and A0 SPLOT with the same manifest/source pins, packed digest, batch order and label counts, and verifies empty unused ranges, finite objectives and dormant MTP separation.
